SOVEREIGN ENTERPRISE — credits and provenance

The spine (canonical envelopes, the verify-before-parse gate, the order-independent materialiser with its role tree,
RGA text, the transparency-log vault, double-entry books, data leases and crypto-shredding, the node, the
deterministic simulator, the AI-native office cost kernel), the AI layer (brain routing and adoption, the mesh,
independent second opinions, the agent rules, the inbound screen, the company kernel and runtime), the live company
and the white paper are original to this build and MIT licensed.

The brains are the Konomi SLM (sjgant80-hub/konomi-slm): knowledge in a verified, readable pattern library — each
pattern earns its place by predicting held-out cases or is cut, and the model answers from a verified pattern or
abstains. The answer path in src/brain.mjs is ported from it. Powered by the Konomi architecture, created by
THOMAS FRUMKIN.

Vendored, verbatim, and credited:
  - vendor/seed-library/seedlib.mjs + sha256.mjs — the seed-library ribosome: grow -> fit -> grade on held-out, the
    seeded RNG, the stratified split and the AUC (seed-library / fall-spore / pattern-organs, sjgant80-hub; the
    SENTINEL-style verify-before-parse guard on seeds).
  - vendor/konomi/domains-ext.mjs — the Konomi SLM's realistic-synthetic domain generators (each a stated rule plus
    seeded noise), with a two-line hook so a device can draw its own sample by seed.

Real data: brains/shopper.sample.json holds held-out (Nov–Dec) sessions of the Online Shoppers Purchasing Intention
dataset — Sakar & Kastro, UCI Machine Learning Repository (2018), DOI 10.24432/C5F88Q, CC BY 4.0.

Standards implemented: Ed25519 (RFC 8032) via WebCrypto; SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4); Merkle transparency logs with
inclusion and consistency proofs (RFC 6962 / RFC 9162); RGA sequence CRDT (Roh et al., 2011); observed-remove sets
and last-writer-wins registers (Shapiro et al., 2011); the Mann–Whitney form of the ROC AUC.

The design lens the estate builds in — entropy-guided regulation (the Guided Entropy Principle), weighted
information pruning (WIPER), behavioural entropy signatures (BES) and dual-map checking — is the work of
GARY W. FLOYD, Lumiea Systems Research Division (a subsidiary of ThunderStruck Service, LLC), New Caney, Texas.

This build draws directly on: Gary W. Floyd, Lumiea Systems Research Division — ThunderStruck Service, LLC —
"From GEP Stabilization to Dual-Map Ethical Reasoning," Derivation v0.2 (Open Defensive Prior Art, Creative
Commons). Its core result — a stable system can stabilise a wrong reference — is why a high-stakes call here must be
confirmed by an INDEPENDENT brain on another device (a copy of the same pattern agreeing proves nothing and is
refused), and why a call no brain can confirm is held for a human (PENDING) rather than forced either way.

